Difference Between Views and Tables
TABLE 
Definition	A physical database object that stores data in rows and columns.	
Storage	Data is physically stored in the table.
Modification	You can insert, update, and delete records directly.

VIEW 
Definition  A virtual table based on the result of a query. It does not store data itself.
Storage  No physical storage; only stores the SQL query definition.
Modification  Usually read-only 


CREATE VIEW StudentView AS
SELECT 
    StudentID,
    FirstName,
    LastName,
    Course,
    Age
FROM StudentDetails;

SELECT * FROM StudentView;
